  "cause": {
    "proximate_text": "torus-to-drywell vacuum breaker 'A' was not set appropriately to prevent mechanical interference from its associated Limit Switches or Closing Magnet Assemblies. This prevented the vacuum breaker from fully seating. Root cause: failure to assess a first-call preventive maintenance (PM) on torus-to-drywell vacuum breakers as high risk, so outage work management processes did not establish readiness milestones, appropriate readiness challenges, and effective risk management actions.",
    "cause_code": "TBD",
    "category": "provisional",
    "theme": "PM risk-classification / outage work management weakness",
    "provisional": true
